  "hypothesis": "Combining A's streaming ring buffer with unrolled loops and manual wraparound, plus the fast scanner shared by B/C, reduces loop overhead and memory latency while preserving O(N^2) time, yielding lower runtime than any single archived transformation.",
  "notes": "Integrated all three source ideas: flat circular row buffer and rolling column sums (A), buffered fread-based integer parsing (B/C). Added unrolling of inner loops and manual ring index wraparound to reduce overhead. No OpenMP used because the streaming dependency across rows prevents parallelization without storing the full matrix; prior measurements show this sequential approach is fastest.",
